# General Project Rules

## Project Structure
```
mono/
├── src/                    # Source files
│   ├── mono/              # Core functionality
│   │   ├── generators/    # SCSS generators
│   │   ├── helpers/      # Helper functions
│   │   └── utils/        # Utility functions
│   ├── examples/          # Example implementations
│   ├── init/             # Initialization templates
│   └── scripts/          # Build and transform scripts
├── local/                 # Local development
└── docs/                  # Documentation
```

## File Settings
- Encoding: UTF-8
- Line endings: LF
- Insert final newline: true
- Trim trailing whitespace: true
- Max line length: 80 characters

## Naming Conventions
- Directories: kebab-case
- Files: kebab-case with appropriate extension
- Documentation: PascalCase.md
- Configuration: kebab-case.json/yml

## Version Control
- Meaningful commit messages
- One feature/fix per commit
- Reference issues/PRs when applicable
- Keep commits atomic and focused
- Use feature branches
- Follow semantic versioning

## Documentation
- README.md in each major directory
- JSDoc/SassDoc for API documentation
- Example usage in code comments
- Update docs with code changes
- Document breaking changes
- Include usage examples

## Dependencies
- Keep dependencies up to date
- Document version requirements
- Use exact versions for critical deps
- Audit dependencies regularly
- Document peer dependencies

## Testing
- Write tests for new features
- Update tests with changes
- Document test requirements
- Use meaningful test names
- Test edge cases

## Build Process
- Document build steps
- Validate output
- Handle errors gracefully
- Provide clean scripts
- Document environment requirements

## Design Tokens
- Follow token naming convention
- Document token structure
- Validate token values
- Keep tokens synchronized
- Document token usage

## Local Development
- Use consistent dev environment
- Document setup steps
- Provide example configurations
- Include dev-only utilities
- Document debugging process

## Error Handling
- Use descriptive messages
- Log appropriately
- Provide recovery steps
- Document known issues
- Include troubleshooting guides

## Performance
- Optimize build output
- Monitor bundle size
- Document performance considerations
- Profile critical paths
- Optimize dependencies

## Security
- Follow security best practices
- Document security considerations
- Keep dependencies secure
- Handle sensitive data appropriately
- Document security requirements

## Accessibility
- Follow WCAG guidelines
- Document a11y features
- Test with screen readers
- Provide a11y documentation
- Include a11y examples
